      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2014 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "Ongoing monocyte infiltration and subsequent macrophage seeding of adipose tissue is thought to be a key feature of obesity pathophysiology. Nagareddy et al. (2014) show that adipose cells locally activate IL-1β in macrophages in part through the alarmin S100A8/A9, which stimulates bone marrow myelopoiesis to perpetuate nonresolving inflammation."
      },
